CLASSIFYING DIFF -- d8g_launch_assert_selftest_candidate.sh
for: dafoam-supervisor.  date: 2026-09-12.  SUPERVISOR CHECK-1 REQUIRED.
FROZEN d8g_launch_assert_selftest.sh NOT TOUCHED; it still passes
against the frozen d8g_run_arm.sh.  NOT COMMITTED.  SUBMISSIONS PARKED.

CLASSIFICATION: MEASUREMENT-SCRIPT CHANGE.  This is the instrument that
proves the launch assertion behaves, so it is handed over as a diff and
not as a summary.

WHY IT HAD TO CHANGE: the old selftest asserted rc 89 in five places.
rc 89 is retired.  A stub that stays alive forever would also HANG the
new code, which no longer stops waiting -- so the stub gains three
tick-driven knobs (FD_FLIP_AFTER, FD_LOG_AFTER, FD_LOG2) that let a
fixture do what a real container does: exit on its own deadline, or
produce its first iteration LATE.  Defaults are empty; every pre-existing
case is byte-identical in behaviour.

THE ONE CHECK THAT MATTERS IS NEW, NOT REWRITTEN: N1b.  A healthy solver
that is merely slow must be LAUNCHED.  There was no such case before,
because under the old contract there could not be one.
